issue.body:
```js
const rfdc = require("rfdc/default");

const original = [1];
original.foo = "bar";
const cloned = rfdc(original);

console.log("original:", original);
console.log("original.length:", original.length);
console.log("cloned:", cloned);
console.log("cloned.length:", cloned.length);
```

You'd expect the output is the same for both of them, but it's not:

```
$ node index.js
original: [ 1, foo: 'bar' ]
original.length: 1
cloned: [ 1, <1 empty item>, foo: 'bar' ]
cloned.length: 2
```

This caused a nasty bug for me when I was accidentally creating weird arrays like this.
